What was adopted: the notification DESIGN only — a settlement-gated "should
notify" evaluator (running / retrying / blocked / failed / aborted / finished;
finished + failed + needs-input notify, aborted dropped), a persisted pending
record keyed per connection + session, completion copy that distinguishes
finished from failed, a non-secret tap-routing payload (session + connection
scope), and periodic background re-checks plus an Android foreground service
for delivery while the app is closed. No code was copied verbatim and no
branding, names, or assets were reused; every file below is an original
implementation written against this repo's own server API and conventions.

Files implementing the adopted design:

- src/lib/session-settlement.ts (+ .test.ts) — settlement classification,
  should-notify rules, shared alert-key scheme and dedupe
- src/stores/session-watch.ts — watch list, periodic/background evaluation
- src/lib/background-poll.ts — expo-background-fetch periodic task
- android/.../SessionMonitorService.kt, SessionMonitorModule.kt,
  SessionMonitorPackage.kt — Android foreground dataSync service + bridge
- src/lib/foreground-service.ts — JS bridge for the service
- src/lib/notifications.ts, app/_layout.tsx — connection-scoped tap routing
